<name>Brake</name>
<section id="1002J_S000U" variety="S000U">
<name>Brake Control</name>
<ttl id="1002J_S000U_744TG_T0089" variety="T0089">
<name>ABS with EBD &amp; TRC &amp; VSC &amp; BA System</name>
<para id="RM00000060B00QX" category="C" type-id="300A2" name-id="442OM-00" from="200612">
<dtccode>C1235/35</dtccode>
<dtcname>Speed Sensor FR Iron Chip Adhesion Malfunction</dtcname>
<dtccode>C1236/36</dtccode>
<dtcname>Speed Sensor FL Iron Chip Adhesion Malfunction</dtcname>
<dtccode>C1238/38</dtccode>
<dtcname>Speed Sensor RR Iron Chip Adhesion Malfunction</dtcname>
<dtccode>C1239/39</dtccode>
<dtcname>Speed Sensor RL Iron Chip Adhesion Malfunction</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM00000060B00QX_05" type-id="33" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00007OP00000">
<name>Function Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>These codes are output when foreign matter adhering to the speed sensor tip or sensor rotor is detected.</ptxt>
<ptxt>The skid control computer determines foreign matter adhesion from abnormalities in the waveform input from the sensor.</ptxt>
<ptxt>These codes may be detected due to malfunctions such as in the connector terminals or wire harness of the speed sensor circuit.</ptxt>
<ptxt>If an iron chip adhesion malfunction code and a speed sensor system malfunction code (C0200/31, C0205/32, C0210/33, C0215/34) are output at the same time, troubleshoot the system malfunction first. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM00000060900ZX"/>)</ptxt>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.42in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="3.08in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="2.58in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC No.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC Detection Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC Output Related Items</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>C1235/35</ptxt>
<ptxt>C1236/36</ptxt>
<ptxt>C1238/38</ptxt>
<ptxt>C1239/39</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>When IG1 terminal voltage is 17.4V or less, at a vehicle speed of 20km/h or more, noise in the sensor signal of the malfunctioning wheel continues for 5 seconds or more</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>When IG1 terminal voltage is 17.4V or less, at a vehicle speed of 10km/h or more, a condition in which noise is input 1 times per 1 rotation of the rotor continues for 15 seconds or more</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Sensor rotor malfunction (foreign matter adhesion, damage)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Foreign matter adhering to speed sensor</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Open or short in speed sensor</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Open or short in wire harness</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Poor connector contact pressure, terminal deformation or corrosion</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Wiring resistance of speed sensor circuit</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Actuator assembly</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM00000060B00QX_06" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00007OQ00000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C161210J01" width="7.106578999in" height="4.7836529in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM00000060B00QX_07" type-id="51" category="05">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM00000060B00QX_08" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM00000060B00QX_08_0013" proc-id="RM0550J___00007OR00000">
<testtitle>Inspect Wire Harness and Connector (Speed Sensor - Actuator Assembly)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Check that the actuator assembly and speed sensor connectors are properly engaged.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Turn the IG OFF and disconnect the actuator assembly and speed sensor connectors.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Check that the connector case and terminals are free of deformation and corrosion.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>No deformation or corrosion</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using the SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance of the wire harness side connectors between the actuator assembly and speed sensor.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C146353J02" width="7.106578999in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
</test1>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="3.47in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.85in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.76in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>7(FR+) - 2(FR+)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry morerows="7" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry morerows="7" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>6(FR-) - 1(FR-)</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>19(FL+) - 2(FL+)</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>18(FL-) - 1(FL-)</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>17(RR+) - 2(RR+)</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>16(RR-) - 1(RR-)</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>5(RL+) - 2(RL+)</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>4(RL-) - 1(RL-)</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using the SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the wire harness side connector of the actuator assembly and body ground.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="3.43in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.88in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.77in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>7 (FR+) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry morerows="7" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry morerows="7" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>10k Ω or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>6 (FR-) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>19 (FL+) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>18 (FL-) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>17 (RR+) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>16 (RR-) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>5 (RL+) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>4 (RL-) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000060B00QX_08_0014" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM00000060B00QX_08_0018" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060B00QX_08_0014" proc-id="RM0550J___00007OS00000">
<testtitle>Inspect ABS &amp; Traction Actuator Assembly (Speed Sensor Power Source)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C146354J01" width="2.775699831in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect the speed sensor connector.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using the SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the wire harness side connector of the speed sensor and body ground.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Voltage</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.23in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="0.91in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="0.99in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>2 (FR+) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry morerows="3" valign="middle">
<ptxt>IG ON</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry morerows="3" valign="middle">
<ptxt>8 to 14V</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>2 (FL+) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>2 (RR+) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>2 (RL+) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000060B00QX_08_0015" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM00000060B00QX_08_0019" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060B00QX_08_0015" proc-id="RM0550J___00007OT00000">
<scantool type="1"/>
<testtitle>Recheck DTC</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Clear the DTCs. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM00000060000PX"/>)</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Turn the IG OFF → ON, drive at a vehicle speed of 20km/h or more for 30 seconds or more, and check that the ABS warning light goes off.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>If the ABS warning light remains on, check the DTCs.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<table frame="all">
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="col1" colwidth="3.17in"/>
<colspec colname="col2" colwidth="0.96in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Malfunction code (2WD models front, 4WD models)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Malfunction code (2WD models rear)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>OK</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>C</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>If the normal code is output, lightly vibrate the connectors and wire harnesses of the actuator and sensors and check that no malfunction code is output.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If a malfunction code is output due to vibration, inspect and repair the connector or wire harness in the relevant area.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000060B00QX_08_0016" fin="false">A</down>
<right ref="RM00000060B00QX_08_0022" fin="true">B</right>
<right ref="RM00000060B00QX_08_0020" fin="true">C</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060B00QX_08_0016" proc-id="RM0550J___00007OU00000">
<testtitle>Inspect Speed Sensor</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Remove the speed sensor of the relevant wheel and check that the tip is free of foreign matter and damage. (For the procedure, refer to <xref label="Seep01" href="RM00000304Y000X"/> [front] and <xref label="Seep02" href="RM000003051000X"/> [rear])</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>No foreign matter or damage</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten3>
<ptxt>When replacing the speed sensor, clean the sensor installation hole before installing it.</ptxt>
</atten3>
<atten4>
<ptxt>When replacing the sensor rotor, replace it together with the axle hub.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</test1>
<table frame="all">
<title>Result</title>
<tgroup cols="2" align="center">
<colspec colname="col1" colwidth="3.14in"/>
<colspec colname="col2" colwidth="0.99in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>OK (front)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>OK (rear)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>NG (front)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>C</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>NG (rear)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>D</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000060B00QX_08_0021" fin="true">A</down>
<right ref="RM00000060B00QX_08_0023" fin="true">B</right>
<right ref="RM00000060B00QX_08_0017" fin="true">C</right>
<right ref="RM00000060B00QX_08_0024" fin="true">D</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060B00QX_08_0017">
<testtitle>Clean or replace speed sensor<xref label="Seep01" href="RM00000304Y000X"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060B00QX_08_0018">
<testtitle>Repair or Replace Wire Harness or Connector</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060B00QX_08_0019">
<testtitle>Replace ABS &amp; Traction Actuator Assembly<xref label="Seep01" href="RM00000304V000X"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060B00QX_08_0020">
<testtitle>Perform Problem Reproduction Test<xref label="Seep01" href="RM000000ABY03DX"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060B00QX_08_0021">
<testtitle>Clean or replace sensor rotor<xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000021S6005X"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060B00QX_08_0022">
<testtitle>Replace Speed Sensor<xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000021SB004X"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060B00QX_08_0023">
<testtitle>Clean or replace sensor rotor<xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000021SH005X"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060B00QX_08_0024">
<testtitle>Clean or replace speed sensor<xref label="Seep01" href="RM000003051000X"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
</subpara>
</para>
</ttl>
</section>
